  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>The hide stays wet in the driest desert and smells of deep water. Its suckers open and close slowly along the sleeves, and they leave ring marks on any table the armor is laid upon.</p><p>You have a +3 bonus to Armor Class while you wear this armor.</p><p>While you wear this armor, you have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed, you can breathe water, and you ignore the pressure and cold of deep water. You cannot be Grappled or Restrained against your will.</p><p><strong>Ink Cloud.</strong> Once per day, as an action, the armor pours out a 30-foot-radius cloud of ink, in water or in air, that lasts for 1 minute. The area is Heavily Obscured for everyone but you. The armor regains this power at dawn.</p><p><strong>The Deep Knows Its Own.</strong> Creatures of the deep sea take the wearer for one of their own. They do not attack unless provoked, and the great ones can be asked one thing: what has passed overhead.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
